<title>BRAZIL: ACPC head has no comment on any export cut accord.</title>
<headline>ACPC head has no comment on any export cut accord.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The president of the Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC) said on Thursday he did not want to comment on whether members had already agreed a minimum cut in coffee exports in the first half of this year.</p>
<p>&quot;I have no comment at this stage,&quot; said Rubens Barbosa, prior to the start of an ACPC meeting.</p>
<p>Earlier, Ugandan Trade and Industry Minister Abel Rwendeire said members had already agreed to a minimum cut and that Thursday would be spent finalising details.</p>
<p>He said the cuts would be not less than one million bags and would involve arabicas and robustas, although mainly robustas.</p>
<p>--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom +55 21 507 4151</p>
